The power delivered by the mirror is proportional to the width of the incident beam that is captured, i.e. to the coordinate \(x_{\max}=R\sin\theta_{\max}\).  
The direct power received without the mirror is proportional to the container diameter \(2a\).  Hence  

\[
\frac{P}{P_0}= \frac{x_{\max}}{a}
        =\frac{R\sin\theta_{\max}}{R\sin\theta_{\max}-\frac{R}{2}\sin2\theta_{\max}}
        =\frac{1}{1-\cos\theta_{\max}}
        =\frac{1}{2\sin^{2}(\theta_{\max}/2)} .
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(\displaystyle \frac{P}{P_0}= \frac{1}{\,1-\cos\theta_{\max}\,}\).
